.TH NVCOMP-GUI 1 "December 2025" "nvCOMP 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nvcomp-gui \- GPU-accelerated compression tool with graphical interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nvcomp-gui
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nvcomp-gui
is a GPU-accelerated compression and decompression tool with a modern Qt6 graphical user interface. It leverages NVIDIA CUDA for high-performance compression with automatic CPU fallback when GPU is unavailable.
.PP
Supported compression algorithms include LZ4, Zstd, Snappy (cross-compatible GPU/CPU), and GDeflate, ANS, Bitcomp (GPU-only). The application supports both single files and directories, with automatic multi-volume splitting for large datasets.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help message and exit
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Display version information and exit
.TP
.B \-\-compress
Start in compression mode
.TP
.B \-\-decompress
Start in decompression mode
.TP
.B \-\-add\-file \fIFILE\fR
Pre-load file into the application
.TP
.B \-\-algorithm \fIALGO\fR
Pre-select compression algorithm (lz4, zstd, snappy, gdeflate, ans, bitcomp)
.TP
.B \-\-cpu
Force CPU mode (disable GPU acceleration)
.TP
.B \-\-volume\-size \fISIZE\fR
Set volume size for multi-volume archives (e.g., 1GB, 500MB, 5GB)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-volumes
Disable multi-volume splitting (create single file)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Launch GUI with file pre-loaded:
.B nvcomp-gui /path/to/file.txt
.TP
Start in compression mode with LZ4:
.B nvcomp-gui --compress --algorithm lz4 /path/to/data/
.TP
Decompress archive:
.B nvcomp-gui --decompress archive.lz4
.SH ALGORITHMS
.TP
.B LZ4
Fast compression with good ratios. Cross-compatible GPU/CPU.
.TP
.B Zstd
Best compression ratios, slower. Cross-compatible GPU/CPU.
.TP
.B Snappy
Fastest compression, lower ratios. Cross-compatible GPU/CPU.
.TP
.B GDeflate
GPU-optimized DEFLATE. GPU-only.
.TP
.B ANS
Asymmetric Numeral Systems. GPU-only.
.TP
.B Bitcomp
Lossless compression for numerical data. GPU-only.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nvCOMP/
User configuration directory
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/nvcomp.desktop
Desktop entry file (user installation)
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/nvcomp.desktop
Desktop entry file (system installation)
.TP
.I /usr/share/nvcomp/
Application data directory
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES
Control which CUDA devices are visible to the application
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Qt platform plugin to use (xcb, wayland, etc.)
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
.B Required
Qt6 (6.2+), Linux kernel 3.2+, glibc 2.31+
.TP
.B Optional
NVIDIA GPU with Compute Capability 7.5+, CUDA Toolkit 11.0+, NVIDIA driver 470+
